# Splashes (docs/briefs/particles.md). Creative mode builds a stone basin
# on the floor between the ledges and fills it with water. Once the water
# has settled, a box thrown down at 10 m/s hits it: the water it hits
# flies up as particles that pass up through the box and come down on
# the pool and on the box. A small box thrown down at 30 m/s splashes
# harder, a plank turned 30 degrees lands on its edge, and a box thrown
# down at 15 m/s onto the sand heap throws the sand up. The conservation
# check counts the cells in flight.
